CORRECTION (2026-09-23): the claim in this message that posting the invoice
mails it to the student is wrong, and was wrong when written.

This commit says: "posting the invoice is what mails it to the student -
through the action_post override in fitness_notifications". That override,
_fitness_notify_invoice, creates an IN-APP notification linking to
/my/invoices/<id>. It sends no email.

Online invoicing is mailed by sale's send_invoice_cron, and that cron
searches payment transactions:

    self.search([('state', '=', 'done'),
                 ('is_post_processed', '=', True), ...])._send_invoice()

A cash sale creates no payment transaction, so it could never be selected -
not on posting, and not later by the cron. Measured on the production
restore: a desk cash sale produced a correct posted invoice and zero
mail.mail rows.

So this commit closed the invoice-CREATION gap and left the invoice-EMAIL
gap open. The inconsistency it set out to remove survived it, one step
further along, until _email_invoice() was added to the desk wizard.

The code here was and is correct; only the message overstated what it did.
